Pulsora's need for a production-grade LLM engineer who can own the full stack from model integration to user-facing product is exactly where my last two years have focused. I built a token-metering and LLM observability platform from scratch, replacing Langfuse, with request-level tracing, audit trails, and five-tier request pricing. Prompt caching cut our LLM token cost by \textbf{roughly 90\%}. That work taught me the operational realities of running LLMs in production, which I believe maps directly to the integration and optimization work this role demands.

